
Tracing level reset from 0 to 1.

Solving 5 * cos(x) ^ 2 - 12 * sin(x) * cos(x) = 2 for x

Tidying to 5 * cos(x) ^ 2 + -12 * sin(x) * cos(x) = 2

5 * cos(x) ^ 2 + -6 * sin(2 * x) = 2

Rewriting equation in terms of cos(x)
gives 5 * cos(x) ^ 2 + -6 * (1 * (2 * cos(x) * (1 - cos(x) ^ 2) ^ (1 / 2))) = 2

Substituting   x1 for cos(x) gives
 -12 * x1 * (1 + -1 * x1 ^ 2) ^ (1/2) + 5 * x1 ^ 2 = 2

Trying to isolate 1 + -1 * x1 ^ 2
 in -12 * x1 * (1 + -1 * x1 ^ 2) ^ (1/2) + 5 * x1 ^ 2 = 2

Assuming -12 * x1 is non-zero

    1 + -1 * x1 ^ 2 = (1/144) * x1 ^ -2 * (2 + -5 * x1 ^ 2) ^ 2
     (by Isolation)

Polynomial 1 + -1 * x1 ^ 2 + (-1/144) * x1 ^ -2 * (2 + -5 * x1 ^ 2) ^ 2 becomes 

(-169/144) * x1 ^ 2 + (41/36) + (-1/36) * x1 ^ -2 when in normal form

Multiply through by x1 ^ 2 to get 

(-169/144) * x1 ^ 4 + (41/36) * x1 ^ 2 + (-1/36) = 0

This is a hidden polynomial in x1 ^ 2

Using quadratic equation formula

Solutions are x1 ^ 2 = (82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2) and x1 ^ 2 = (82/169) + (-72/169) * (-1 * (7/6) ^ (1/2))

    x1 = ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # x1 = -1 * ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # x1 = ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # x1 = -1 * ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)
     (by Isolation)

Applying substitution 
    x1 = cos(x)

   to    : 
    x1 = ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # x1 = -1 * ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # x1 = ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # x1 = -1 * ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)

   gives : 
    cos(x) = ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # cos(x) = -1 * ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # cos(x) = ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2) # cos(x) = -1 * ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)



Solving disjunct cos(x) = ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)

	Letting n1 denote an arbitrary integer
    x = arccos(((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n1 # x = -1 * arccos(((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n1
     (by Isolation)


Solving disjunct cos(x) = -1 * ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)

	Letting n2 denote an arbitrary integer
    x = arccos(-1 * ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n2 # x = -1 * arccos(-1 * ((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n2
     (by Isolation)


Solving disjunct cos(x) = ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)

	Letting n3 denote an arbitrary integer
    x = arccos(((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n3 # x = -1 * arccos(((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n3
     (by Isolation)


Solving disjunct cos(x) = -1 * ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)

	Letting n4 denote an arbitrary integer
    x = arccos(-1 * ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n4 # x = -1 * arccos(-1 * ((82/169) + (72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2)) + 360 * n4
     (by Isolation)

Answer is : 
(X1 # (X2 # (X3 # (X4 # (X5 # (X6 # (X7 # X8)))))))
  where :
    X1 =  x = 360 * n1 + arccos(((82/169) + (-72/169) * (7/6) ^ (1/2)) ^ (1/2))
